ue" :db/id 17592186364956} {:answer/id #uuid "2a2581fc-f5d1-56c8-ab61-5d417f0d30e1" :answer/type {:db/id 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I and III only" :db/id 17592186364957} {:answer/id #uuid "14d9082f-208d-5d34-9c63-524f45f1904f" :answer/type {:db/id 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I only" :db/id 17592186364958} {:answer/id #uuid "f9c099fe-52bc-5e28-83a9-4aad7f968450" :answer/type {:db/id 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "III only" :db/id 17592186364959} {:answer/id #uuid "df4cf5da-869a-50b7-a8cd-35b980cbe9eb" :answer/type {:db/id 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II only" :db/id 17592186364960}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "f9c099fe-52bc-5e28-83a9-4aad7f968450" :answer/type {:db/id 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "III only" :db/id 17592186364959} :answer-field/id #uuid "b43375d0-11ca-5e43-8be7-2100aee7f584" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id 17592186364955}] :question/difficulty {:db/id 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "d0d9bc49-c94e-5174-9068-2abf75c42684" :question/math-academy-id "q-128490" :question/problem "Which of the following statements are true regarding the matrix $M$ given below?\n\n- $det(M)=10$\n- $det(M)=-5$\n- $M$ is a singular matrix\n\n \n\n$$\nM=[\\begin{aligned}\\sqrt{5} & 0 & \\frac{1}{3} \\\\ 0 & 3 & 5 \\\\ -3\\sqrt{5} & 3 & 4\\end{aligned}]\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Remember that a square matrix is singular if its determinant is equal to $0.$\n\nUsing the formula, we take the alternating sum of the entries in the top row of the matrix, multiplied by their respective minors, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(M) & =|\\begin{aligned}\\sqrt{5} & 0 & \\frac{1}{3} \\\\ 0 & 3 & 5 \\\\ -3\\sqrt{5} & 3 & 4\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =\\sqrt{5}|\\begin{aligned}3 & 5 \\\\ 3 & 4\\end{aligned}|-0|\\begin{aligned}0 & 5 \\\\ -3\\sqrt{5} & 4\\end{aligned}|+\\frac{1}{3}|\\begin{aligned}0 & 3 \\\\ -3\\sqrt{5} & 3\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =\\sqrt{5}(12-15)-0+\\frac{1}{3}(0+9\\sqrt{5}) \\\\  & =\\sqrt{5}\\cdot (-3)+\\frac{1}{3}\\cdot 9\\sqrt{5} \\\\  & =-3\\sqrt{5}+3\\sqrt{5} \\\\  & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nSince $det(M)=0$, the matrix is singular. \n\nTherefore, only statement III is true."}] [{:db/id 17592186060446 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id 17592186059849 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "ab642ad6-d9e0-5734-83b4-81627b9132eb" :knowledge-point/title "Solving for an Unknown Given the Determinant"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "b1912b5b-58a0-5491-a50c-b728a4ed3e22" :answer/type {:db/id 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$5$ and $6$ only" :db/id 17592186059299} {:answer/id #uuid "c8f7c0b0-c3a5-549e-b078-15d79f0248eb" :answer/type {:db/id 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$2$ and $8$ only" :db/id 17592186059300} {:answer/id #uuid "06c85cfe-b123-504b-9faf-324c33d747ac" :answer/type {:db/id 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$8$ only" :db/id 17592186059301} {:answer/id #uuid "0e43444a-08a5-579c-96df-f1622d1ebfa6" :answer/type {:db/id 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$-8$ and $-2$ only" :db/id 17592186059302} {:answer/id #uuid "38b74efe-eb9e-5251-9500-fed3d79db7a2" :answer/type {:db/id 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$5$ only" :db/id 17592186059303}] :answer-field/id #uuid "252ad927-f137-587e-abae-e173b3313976" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id 17592186059298}] :question/id #uuid "f04c86de-5ed5-52ee-bc8b-1a0c07c06519" :question/math-academy-id "q-9657" :question/problem "Given that the determinant of\n$\\begin{bmatrix}2 & -1 & 3 \\\\ x & 2 & 4 \\\\ -2 & 1 & x + 3\\end{bmatrix}$\nis $8$, find all the possible val